    <briefdescription>
<para>A trivial type to allow construction of constexpr <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_align" kindref="compound">Align</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is currently needed to workaround a bug in GCC 5.3 which prevents definition of constexpr assign operators. <ulink url="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/46756288/explicitly-defaulted-function-cannot-be-declared-as-constexpr-because-the-implic">https://stackoverflow.com/questions/46756288/explicitly-defaulted-function-cannot-be-declared-as-constexpr-because-the-implic</ulink> FIXME: Remove this, make all assign operators constexpr and introduce user defined literals when we don&apos;t have to support GCC 5.3 anymore. <ulink url="https://llvm.org/docs/GettingStarted.html#getting-a-modern-host-c-toolchain">https://llvm.org/docs/GettingStarted.html#getting-a-modern-host-c-toolchain</ulink> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
